WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.000
Part 2. You will hear a town councillor reporting on the local transport network and a recreation facility.

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:13.000
First, you have some time to look at questions 11 to 14.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:50.000
Now listen carefully and answer questions 11 to 14.

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:56.000
Right, next on the agenda we have traffic and highways. Councillor Thornton.

00:00:56.000 --> 00:01:04.000
Thank you. Well, we now have the results of the survey carried out last month about traffic and road transport in the town.

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:08.000
People were generally satisfied with the state of the roads.

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:12.000
There were one or two complaints about potholes, which will be addressed,

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:21.000
but a significant number of people complained about the increasing number of heavy vehicles using our local roads to avoid traffic elsewhere.

00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:30.000
We'd expected more complaints by commuters about the reduction in the train service, but it doesn't seem to have affected people too much.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:40.000
The cycle path that runs alongside the river is very well used by both cyclists and pedestrians since the surface was improved last year,

00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:46.000
but overtaking can be a problem, so we're going to add a bit on the side to make it wider.

00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:56.000
At some stage, we'd like to extend the path so that it goes all the way through the town, but that won't be happening in the immediate future.

00:01:56.000 --> 00:02:04.000
The plans to have a pedestrian crossing next to the post office have unfortunately had to be put on hold for the time being.

00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:11.000
We'd budgeted for this to be done this financial year, but then there were rumours that the post office was going to move,

00:02:11.000 --> 00:02:15.000
which would have meant there wasn't really a need for a crossing.

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:23.000
Now they've confirmed that they're staying where they are, but the highways department have told us that it would be dangerous to have a pedestrian crossing

00:02:23.000 --> 00:02:29.000
where we'd originally planned it, as there's a bend in the road there, so that'll need some more thought.

00:02:29.000 --> 00:02:37.000
On Station Road, near the station and level crossing, drivers can face quite long waits if the level crossing's closed,

00:02:37.000 --> 00:02:43.000
and we've now got signs up requesting them not to leave their engines running at that time.

00:02:43.000 --> 00:02:50.000
This means pedestrians waiting on the pavement to cross the railway line don't have to breathe in car fumes.

00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:56.000
We've had some problems with cyclists leaving their bikes chained to the railings outside the ticket office,

00:02:56.000 --> 00:03:00.000
but the station has agreed to provide bike racks there.

00:03:02.000 --> 00:03:10.000
Before you hear the rest of the talk, you have some time to look at questions 15 to 20.

00:03:13.000 --> 00:03:18.000
Now listen and answer questions 15 to 20.

00:03:44.000 --> 00:03:54.000
So next on the agenda is proposals for improvements to the recreation ground. Councillor Thornton again.

00:03:54.000 --> 00:04:04.000
Well, since we managed to extend the recreation ground, we've spent some time talking to local people about how it could be made a more attractive and useful space.

00:04:05.000 --> 00:04:13.000
If you have a look at the map up on the screen, you can see the river up in the north and the community hall near the entrance from the road.

00:04:13.000 --> 00:04:22.000
At present, cars can park between the community hall and that line of trees to the east, but this is quite dangerous for pedestrians,

00:04:22.000 --> 00:04:28.000
so we're suggesting a new car park on the opposite side of the community hall, right next to it.

00:04:29.000 --> 00:04:32.000
We also have a new location for the cricket pitch.

00:04:32.000 --> 00:04:38.000
As we've now purchased additional space to the east of the recreation ground, beyond the trees,

00:04:38.000 --> 00:04:47.000
we plan to move it away from its current location, which is rather near the road, into this new area beyond the line of trees.

00:04:47.000 --> 00:04:52.000
This means there's less danger of stray balls hitting cars or pedestrians.

00:04:52.000 --> 00:05:00.000
We've got plans for a children's playground, which will be accessible by a footpath from the community hall and will be alongside the river.

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:06.000
We'd originally thought of having it close to the road, but we think this will be a more attractive location.

00:05:06.000 --> 00:05:12.000
The skateboard ramp is very popular with both younger and older children.

00:05:12.000 --> 00:05:20.000
We had considered moving this up towards the river, but in the end, we decided to have it in the southeast corner near the road.

00:05:21.000 --> 00:05:26.000
The pavilion is very well used at present by both football players and cricketers.

00:05:26.000 --> 00:05:34.000
It will stay where it is now, to the left of the line of trees and near to the river, handy for both the football and cricket pitches.

00:05:34.000 --> 00:05:39.000
And finally, we'll be getting a new notice board for local information,

00:05:39.000 --> 00:05:45.000
and that will be directly on people's right as they go from the road into the recreation ground.

00:05:50.000 --> 00:05:55.000
You now have half a minute to check your answers to part two.

00:06:20.000 --> 00:06:21.000
Thank you.

